  "notes": "Built from the real archived 2024-25 bulletin (https://bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2024-2025/undergraduate/colleges/bellisario-communications/journalism-ba/), raw HTML fetched and parsed directly, cross-checked against the page's own printed subtotals (Total Credits 120; semester subtotals 15/16/16/15/15/15/14.5/13.5 all reconciled). 2024 is a real transitional year between the 2022/2023 shape and the 2025/2026 shape: COMM 205 is STILL not a Common Requirement for the Major this year (Common Requirements prescribed courses still totaled 13cr, and the Digital and Print Option is still an 18-credit option with two real 'select 6 credits' elective pools, same as 2022/2023 -- this only changed starting 2025-26) -- but the university's General Education relabeling had already taken effect by this catalog year: COMM 271 moved to Fall (Semester 1, alongside COMM 160), the Gen Ed labels switched from 'Foreign Language'/'GEN ED (GH)(Inter-Domain)'/'GEN ED (GS)(Inter-Domain)' to 'World Language'/a domain-generic 'GEN ED (Inter-Domain)', a new 'GEN ED (Exploration)' category appears (Semester 3 and Semester 6), and 'Other Cultures' became 'World Cultures' -- all matching the 2025/2026 file's labeling exactly one year early, while the major-specific requirement (COMM 205, option credit total) had not yet changed. The first elective pool ('Print Elective': 269, 362, 364, 402, 461, 462, 463, 464W, 474, 481, 495) matches 2023 and the current 2026 plan unchanged. The second elective pool ('Print/Digital Elective') dropped COMM 381 this year -- confirmed by inspecting the raw HTML: COMM 381 appears in the 2024 bulletin's course list as a bare, unlinked, titleless entry (no href, no course title, exactly the same unlinked-placeholder pattern documented for COMM 407C in the 2022 file's notes), unlike its real linked/titled listing in the 2023 bulletin -- so it was excluded here as not a genuinely offered course, leaving 180, 205, 401, 405, 407A, 407B, 410, 411, 412, 419, 494H, 496, 499.",
